      "Language": "cze",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Thirty-five selected patients with unstable angina were divided at random into group T (n = 17 treated by thrombolysis and group K (K = 18) which served as control. In the group treated by thrombolysis new myocardial infarction developed less frequently (T = 3/17, K = 8/18). In patients without a new myocardial infarction in group T indirect signs of a more favourable coronary flow were found, as compared with the control group. Patients treated by thrombolysis where later an infarction developed had an insignificantly higher left ventricular ejection fraction (40%:35%)."},
